    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for pet owners. The endpoint is `POST /api/owners` (create) with the value read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the `title` had to be persisted for the salutation to survive to the GET response.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added an optional `title` string field to `OwnerFields` (request input, documented as MR/MRS/MS/DR).\n   - Added a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 added a `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (all four: hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table. Seed inserts list columns explicitly, so appending is safe.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping and a `salutation(owner)` helper: `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is present. `title` maps automatically from request DTO to entity via MapStruct.\n\n5. **`ApplyOwner.java`** \u2014 copied `title` on updates too (PUT), for consistency.\n\nThe `Cp45Tests` acceptance test (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 salutation `DR who`) passes, and the full suite of 56 tests remains green.",
